Ans :

bool thread_mlfqs : This is global boolean variable. If it is set to true, it activates the Multi-Level Feedback Queue Scheduler (MLFQS). The kernel option -mlfqs is used to control it during startup.
int recent_cpu : This is  structured member in struct thread. It tracks a thread's recent CPU utilization, which the 4.4BSD scheduler uses to determine a thread's priority. 
int nice : This is  structured member in struct thread. It stores the "nice" value for a thread, which influences its priority in the 4.4BSD scheduler. The thread is less favorable to run when the nice value is higher.
fixed_point_t load_avg : It monitors the average load across the system, which affects how the MLFQS recalculates thread priorities and recent CPU utilization.

